    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Webhook intake + validation\nPOST JSON to /webhook/lead-intake. The Code node trims, lower-cases and length-limits fields, checks required fields and email format, and flags bots via a hidden `website` honeypot. Invalid payloads get a 400 with error details; valid ones get an immediate 202 so your site never waits on the AI.",
        "height": 680,
        "width": 960
      },
      "id": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000100",
      "name": "Note: Intake",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Claude scoring (tool use)\nClaude is forced to call one tool with a strict JSON schema: category, 0-100 score, use case, next action, reply subject + body. No regex-scraping of prose. The Code node still clamps and whitelists every field. Retries: 4 tries, 4 s apart.",
        "height": 500,
        "width": 500
      },
      "id": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000101",
      "name": "Note: Claude",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1140,
        -40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Route + Slack approval\nSpam is discarded, score < 50 goes straight to HubSpot as a nurture contact, score >= 50 is posted to #lead-approvals with Approve & Send / Decline buttons. Approvals auto-expire after 48 h.",
        "height": 820,
        "width": 720
      },
      "id": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000102",
      "name": "Note: Approval",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1660,
        -200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. Act on approval\nOnly after a human clicks Approve: the contact is upserted in HubSpot as a lead, and the exact reviewed draft is emailed to the prospect via Gmail.",
        "height": 500,
        "width": 480
      },
      "id": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000103",
      "name": "Note: Action",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2400,
        -40
      ]
    }
